>, <name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Hanson</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Lund</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name> (<year>2006</year>) <article-title>Acute nephrotoxic and obstructive injury primes the kidney to endotoxin-driven cytokine/chemokine production</article-title>. <source>Kidney Int</source><volume>69</volume>: <fpage>1181</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1188</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16395275</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Nath1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Nath</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Grande</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Farrugia</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Croatt</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Belcher</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2013</year>) <article-title>Age sensitizes the kidney to heme protein-induced acute kidney injury</article-title>. <source>Am J Physiol</source><volume>304</volume>: <fpage>F317</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>325</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Zager5"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Zager</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Alpers</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name> (<year>1989</year>) <article-title>Effects of aging on expression of ischemic acute renal failure in rats</article-title>. <source>Lab Invest</source><volume>61</volume>: <fpage>290</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>294</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2770246</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Zager6"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Zager</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Naito</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Lund</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2008</year>) <article-title>Growth and development alter susceptibility to acute renal injury</article-title>. <source>Kidney Int</source><volume>74</volume>: <fpage>674</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>678</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18563055</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Nath2"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Nath</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Balla</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Vercellotti</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Balla</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Jacob</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>1992</year>) <article-title>Induction of heme oxygenase is a rapid, protective response in rhabdomyolysis in the rat</article-title>. <source>J Clin Invest</source><volume>90</volume>: <fpage>267</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>270</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1634613</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Jarmi1"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Jarmi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Agarwal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name> (<year>2009</year>) <article-title>Heme oxygenase and renal disease</article-title>. <source>Curr Hypertens Rep</source><volume>11</volume>: <fpage>56</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19146802</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0066776-Ruiz1"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Ruiz S, Pergola PE, Zager RA, Vaziri ND (2013) Targeting the transcription factor Nrf2 to ameliorate oxidative stress and inflammation in chronic kidney disease. Kidney Int Jan 16. 10.1038/ki.2012.439.</mixed-citation></ref><r